Both base URLs are HTTPS (`lib/WWW/VastAI.pm:28` `https://console.vast.ai`, `:43` `https://run.vast.ai`). `cpanfile` requires `LWP::UserAgent` and `HTTP::Request` but not `LWP::Protocol::https`, which is a separate distribution. On a clean install the first call comes back as LWP's internal `501 Protocol scheme 'https' is not supported (LWP::Protocol::https not installed)`, which `_parse_response` turns into `Vast.ai API error: 501 Protocol scheme ...` at best.

p5-www-metaforge fixed the same thing in its k5.

Done when: `cpanfile` requires `LWP::Protocol::https`.

